WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.250
Many organizations generate SBOMs during software builds, release processes,

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.300
and deployment activities.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.851
Integrating SBOM generation into development workflows can improve consistency and reduce manual effort.

00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:13.051
The software development lifecycle is a natural place to create SBOMs because

00:00:13.051 --> 00:00:15.152
build systems often know which packages,

00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:18.302
libraries, containers, and artifacts were included in a release.

00:00:18.302 --> 00:00:20.052
Automation helps keep SBOMs current.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:24.253
If an SBOM is generated every time software is built or released,

00:00:24.253 --> 00:00:28.103
the inventory is more likely to reflect what was actually delivered.

00:00:28.103 --> 00:00:30.903
SBOMs can also be stored with release artifacts.

00:00:30.903 --> 00:00:35.104
This makes it easier to connect a product version to the components

00:00:35.104 --> 00:00:37.904
that were present at the time of release.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:41.054
Development teams can use SBOMs to review dependency changes.

00:00:41.054 --> 00:00:43.155
A new package, major version change,

00:00:43.155 --> 00:00:46.655
or unexpected transitive dependency may deserve additional review before release.

00:00:46.655 --> 00:00:51.556
Security teams can use SBOM outputs to enrich vulnerability management and software risk workflows.

00:00:51.556 --> 00:00:56.806
Compliance teams may use the same data to support evidence requests or customer assurance processes.

00:00:56.806 --> 00:01:02.407
The practical lesson is to make SBOM generation part of how software is built and maintained.

00:01:02.407 --> 00:01:04.857
When SBOMs are embedded in the lifecycle,

00:01:04.857 --> 00:01:08.007
they become living operational artifacts rather than occasional documents.

00:01:08.007 --> 00:01:11.508
Teams should also decide how SBOMs are versioned and retained.

00:01:11.508 --> 00:01:15.708
Being able to connect a released product version to the SBOM generated

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:19.909
for that release can be critical during vulnerability response or customer assurance

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:20.559
work.

00:01:20.559 --> 00:01:22.659
Lifecycle integration also makes ownership clearer.

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:27.209
If each product team knows where its SBOMs are created, stored, and reviewed,

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:31.460
software transparency becomes a repeatable engineering practice rather than an occasional special request.
